 "category": "both",
 "summary": "FlowVision is a native, open-source macOS image viewer built around a waterfall/justified thumbnail layout and Finder-like file management. It is tuned for very large folders, plays native Mac video formats, and adds a recursive mode, Finder tags, ratings and mouse gestures for jumping between folders.",
 "where_it_wins": [
  "Waterfall and justified thumbnail layouts",
  "Right-click mouse gestures to jump between folders",
  "Finder tags and XMP ratings with filters",
  "HDR display",
  "Profiles for layout presets",
  "Runs on macOS 11+"
 ],
 "where_schnellbild_wins": [
  "Plays MKV, WebM, AVI etc. internally via VLC instead of handing off to another player",
  "Subtitles, audio-track choice and a movable control bar",
  "Archives and comics (ZIP/RAR/7z, CBZ/CBR) as folders",
  "Two-pane file manager with F5/F6 and undo",
  "App Sandbox",
  "Fully customisable keyboard shortcuts with printable cheat sheet",
  "Playlist on the fly in the slideshow"
 ],
